---
layout: changelog
title: "Force every user in a project to reset their password"
date: 2026-11-13
cover: /images/blog/announcing-force-password-reset/cover.avif
tags: auth, security, console, api
---

You can now require every user in a project to choose a new password with [force password reset](/docs/products/auth/security#force-password-reset). Use it when passwords may have leaked, for example after a data breach or a credential-stuffing attack.

Click **Reset all passwords** under **Auth** > **Settings** > **Security actions** in the Appwrite Console, or call the Project service's `deletePasswords` method with an API key that has the `users.write` scope. From then on, an email and password sign-in with an older password fails with `user_password_reset_required` until the user sets a new password through password recovery. Existing sessions stay active, so pair it with **Force sign out** when sessions may be compromised too.

The reset applies instantly at any project size. Users without a password, users who sign up afterwards, and API keys are not affected. 

